  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Cyclone Yaku in Rio Seco (Cieneguilla, Lima-Peru)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Cyclone Yaku hit Peru at the beginning of March 2023. The  Peruvian National Meteorological and Hydrological Service (SENAMHI) described it as as an &quot;unorganised tropical cyclone&quot; not seen since 1983 or 1998.  Yaku impacted the life of many Peruvians, among them, the 2500 families of Rio Seco in Cieneguilla (Lima).  Rio Seco&apos;s population is settled in the ravines of the area. The mudslides originated by Cyclone have destroyed their houses and leave them with nothing: no house, food or clothes.</narrative>
  </description>
